-- title:
--   Stalk at a smooth generic point of the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, and let $\varpi_0 \in A_0$ be an element with $\mathfrak m_{A_0} = (\varpi_0)$. Let $X_0$ be a scheme together with a morphism $\mathrm{toBase}_0 \colon X_0 \to \operatorname{Spec} A_0$, and assume $X_0$ is integral and that $\mathrm{toBase}_0$ is flat and locally of finite presentation. Let $\eta_0 \in X_0$ be a point whose image under the underlying map of $\mathrm{toBase}_0$ is the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_0$, lying in the smooth locus of $\mathrm{toBase}_0$, and suppose that every $\zeta \in X_0$ which specialises to $\eta_0$ and lies over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_0$ is equal to $\eta_0$ (that is, $\eta_0$ admits no proper generisation inside the special fibre). Then the local ring $\mathcal O_{X_0,\eta_0}$, the stalk of the structure presheaf of $X_0$ at $\eta_0$, is a discrete valuation ring, and its maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_0$ under the composite of the inverse of the canonical isomorphism $A_0 \xrightarrow{\sim} \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} A_0)$, the map on global sections induced by $\mathrm{toBase}_0$, and the germ map $\Gamma(X_0) \to \mathcal O_{X_0,\eta_0}$ at $\eta_0$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that a flat, finitely presented model over a discrete valuation ring has a discrete valuation ring as local ring at a smooth generic point of its special fibre, with the uniformiser of the base serving as uniformiser upstairs. It feeds into [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_valuationSubring_eq_range_stalk_of_iso_pullback_of_mem_smoothLocus_of_isDiscreteValuationRing_of_specializes`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_valuationSubring_eq_range_stalk_of_iso_pullback_of_mem_smoothLocus_of_isDiscreteValuationRing_of_specializes), where such stalks are identified with valuation subrings.
